  "prompt": "Prove that there is a natural number $n$ with $11 \\mid (2^n - 1)$. This is an existence statement, so one example proves it. In this book $\\mathbb{N} = \\{1, 2, 3, \\dots\\}$, so $n$ must be positive.",
