  "answer": "n = 10",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Compute 2ⁿ − 1 for n = 1, 2, 3, … and check which is a multiple of 11.",
    "Working mod 11: 2⁵ = 32 ≡ −1, so 2¹⁰ ≡ 1."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Take $n = 10$: $2^{10} - 1 = 1023 = 11 \\cdot 93$, so $11 \\mid (2^{10} - 1)$.",
    "So such an $n$ exists. $\\blacksquare$"
